WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:03.300
- [Narrator] This was Snap's
trajectory for most of 2021.

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:05.460
It's share value was steadily moving up

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:07.380
and the company was posting record revenue

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:09.049
and launching new initiatives.

00:00:09.049 --> 00:00:11.310
- Off the grid and off the leash!

00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:13.680
- [Narrator] By September, its
stock price had skyrocketed

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:17.070
over 700% from its low point in 2020.

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:21.180
But in October, 2021,
Snap's stock began to slip.

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:24.750
Since then, its share
value has fallen over 80%

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:26.460
and in August, Snap announced-

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:28.350
- That they will cut
20% of their workforce.

00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:31.410
- Discontinue investments
in Snap Originals,

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:33.660
minis, games, and Pixy.

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:35.313
- [Narrator] So what went wrong?

00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:38.760
It all started in April, 2021.

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:42.750
- Apple announced these
changes to its privacy policy

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:45.840
that said apps now have to ask users

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:47.190
if they wanna be tracked.

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:49.140
- [Narrator] According to
mobile app analytics provider,

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:51.420
Flurry, US users opt into tracking

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:53.250
only about 16% of the times

00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:55.110
they encounter Apple's privacy prompt.

00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:57.330
This makes it more
difficult for advertisers

00:00:57.330 --> 00:00:59.220
to target their ads at the right audience

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:02.550
and get information about
how well their ads performed.

00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:05.370
The impact of Apple's changes
showed up six months later

00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:08.160
when Snap posted revenue
growth numbers that fell short

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:10.470
of what investors and
analysts were expecting.

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:12.480
Its stock price dropped over 20%

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:15.000
in after hours trading that day.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:17.640
Other social media companies
like Facebook's parent, Meta,

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:19.890
also took a hit from
Apple's privacy changes.

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:21.630
But Snap is a smaller company

00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:24.090
that brings in less revenue to begin with.

00:01:24.090 --> 00:01:26.400
Investors got a glimmer
of hope in February

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:29.010
when Snap posted its first
ever quarterly profit

00:01:29.010 --> 00:01:30.180
as a public company.

00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:32.490
But it was short lived
because a few weeks later-

00:01:32.490 --> 00:01:35.220
- The Russian invasion has begun.

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:37.590
- [Narrator] The first of a
myriad of compounding factors

00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:40.980
that contributed to Snap's
continued decline in 2022.

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:43.080
Snap says it spent $5 million

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:44.730
helping its team members in Ukraine.

00:01:44.730 --> 00:01:47.130
And as macroeconomic
conditions deteriorated,

00:01:47.130 --> 00:01:49.050
advertisers pulled back spending.

00:01:49.050 --> 00:01:51.420
- Snapchat, while it might be a place

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:53.940
where advertisers are
indeed putting their money

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:55.860
when they have money to spend,

00:01:55.860 --> 00:01:58.410
it might be one of the
things that's gonna get cut

00:01:58.410 --> 00:01:59.790
when they're trying to pull back.

00:01:59.790 --> 00:02:02.910
Meta, which owns Facebook and Instagram,

00:02:02.910 --> 00:02:05.550
which have slightly older user bases,

00:02:05.550 --> 00:02:09.540
it's gonna provide better
returns generally for advertisers

00:02:09.540 --> 00:02:12.690
because older people are gonna
have more disposable income.

00:02:12.690 --> 00:02:14.550
- [Narrator] Snap was
also hit particularly hard

00:02:14.550 --> 00:02:16.260
because the company relies primarily

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:18.090
on direct response advertising,

00:02:18.090 --> 00:02:19.890
which are ads that are
intended to get users

00:02:19.890 --> 00:02:21.940
to immediately click on or buy something.

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:24.630
Snap says this type of advertising

00:02:24.630 --> 00:02:27.030
is easy to turn on and
off and to scale quickly

00:02:27.030 --> 00:02:29.370
with high return on
investment for advertisers.

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:30.750
- [Derek] But that works
in the opposite way

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:32.490
when folks have to retrench their budgets,

00:02:32.490 --> 00:02:34.020
and it's very easy to shrink down.

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:35.850
- [Narrator] Snap
doesn't report its ad mix

00:02:35.850 --> 00:02:38.220
but has said that a significant
majority of its revenue

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:39.663
is direct response related.

00:02:41.790 --> 00:02:43.620
This disruption in the digital ad market

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:45.240
plus Apple's privacy changes,

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:46.680
the broad effects of inflation,

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:48.300
and labor and supply chain issues,

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:50.190
all sent Snap over the edge.

00:02:50.190 --> 00:02:51.630
- If it was one thing,

00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:53.850
Snap might have been able to handle it.

00:02:53.850 --> 00:02:56.460
But when you have all these
different things happening

00:02:56.460 --> 00:03:00.030
at once, Snap's just getting
hit one thing after the other,

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:02.250
that's where the company
started to struggle.

00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:04.800
- [Narrator] In the spring,
Snap continued adding staff

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:06.000
and launching new initiatives,

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:07.350
including a camera drone.

00:03:07.350 --> 00:03:09.930
- [Announcer] This is Pixy,
a pocket-sized, friendly,

00:03:09.930 --> 00:03:11.160
free-flying camera.

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:12.060
- [Narrator] And a content push

00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:13.920
for its Originals scripted videos.

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:16.890
- [Simone] This is "Daring Simone Biles."

00:03:16.890 --> 00:03:18.180
- [Narrator] Despite its new products,

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:20.460
Snap's share value continued to tumble,

00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:22.590
and in late May Snap told investors

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:24.990
that its revenue growth numbers
were likely going to come in

00:03:24.990 --> 00:03:26.640
lower than expected.

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:29.550
- Profit warnings are not
something that companies

00:03:29.550 --> 00:03:31.260
just give out willy-nilly,

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:33.390
and so the fact that they did this

00:03:33.390 --> 00:03:35.700
was quite a big deal actually.

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:36.960
- [Narrator] Following this announcement,

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:38.940
Snap slowed hiring and spending.

00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:41.610
The company had previously
added staff at breakneck speed

00:03:41.610 --> 00:03:42.660
during the pandemic,

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:46.830
growing its headcount by around
65% since the end of 2020.

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:48.600
Snap also brought on two executives

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:50.280
to specifically address the challenges

00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:51.750
from Apple's privacy changes.

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:53.850
But analysts say they still expect Snap

00:03:53.850 --> 00:03:56.340
to post a hefty net loss this quarter.

00:03:56.340 --> 00:03:57.840
In August, Snap announced

00:03:57.840 --> 00:03:59.550
it was shutting down future development

00:03:59.550 --> 00:04:01.110
of its flying selfie drone, Pixy,

00:04:01.110 --> 00:04:03.660
which it had launched less
than four months earlier.

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:05.850
- And then two weeks later they announced

00:04:05.850 --> 00:04:08.340
that they were gonna lay
off 20% of their staff

00:04:08.340 --> 00:04:10.410
and shut down many more projects

00:04:10.410 --> 00:04:13.080
that weren't core to its business.

00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:14.370
- [Narrator] Around that same time,

00:04:14.370 --> 00:04:16.485
Netflix poached Snap's
Chief Business Officer

00:04:16.485 --> 00:04:18.870
and Vice President of
Sales for the Americas

00:04:18.870 --> 00:04:21.300
to kickstart its ad-supported
subscription plan.

00:04:21.300 --> 00:04:23.070
Snap declined to comment.

00:04:23.070 --> 00:04:24.780
At the Code Conference in September,

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:26.700
Snap CEO responded to questions

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:28.590
about a possible takeover saying-

00:04:28.590 --> 00:04:30.030
- I believe that the best way

00:04:30.030 --> 00:04:32.280
to realize our long-term potential

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:34.710
is by building an independent company.

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:36.810
And I think while the
stock price has gone up

00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:37.920
and down over time,

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:40.200
we have slowly and steadily increased

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:42.570
the long-term value of our business.

00:04:42.570 --> 00:04:44.040
- [Narrator] Looking ahead, Snap says

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:45.660
it expects the cost-cutting measures

00:04:45.660 --> 00:04:49.590
to reduce the company's annual
costs by around $500 million.

00:04:49.590 --> 00:04:52.440
Snap says it's also working
to diversify its ad business

00:04:52.440 --> 00:04:54.270
by monetizing features like Spotlight,

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:56.493
which tries to appeal to content creators.

00:04:58.050 --> 00:05:00.990
Snap says it's also working
to monetize My Places,

00:05:00.990 --> 00:05:03.300
which offers users
personalized recommendations

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:05.040
of places to eat and visit.

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:07.230
The company also launched Snapchat Plus,

00:05:07.230 --> 00:05:09.030
a subscription service that gives users

00:05:09.030 --> 00:05:12.690
early and exclusive access
to features for 3.99 a month.

00:05:12.690 --> 00:05:15.180
- Analysts, investors, myself,

00:05:15.180 --> 00:05:17.370
we're all watching to see,

00:05:17.370 --> 00:05:20.193
is the digital ad business recovering?

00:05:21.090 --> 00:05:23.790
Are they diversifying their business?

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:26.490
If something happens again
to the digital ad market,

00:05:26.490 --> 00:05:28.503
will it not affect them
as much in the future?

00:05:28.503 --> 00:05:31.170
- [Narrator] Snap has been
through difficult times before.

00:05:31.170 --> 00:05:33.783
The question again is
whether it can snap back.

